### Phase 3: Hardware Integration (Current = ~50%)

#### 3.1 Supported Boards

| Board | Stage Mode | Upload Mode | Priority |
|-------|------------|-------------|----------|
| Arduino Uno | ✅ | ✅ | High |
| Arduino Nano | ❌ | ❌ | High |
| Arduino Mega | ❌ | ❌ | Medium |
| ESP32 | ❌ | ❌ | High |
| ESP8266 | ❌ | ❌ | Medium |

#### 3.2 Hardware Blocks (Upload Mode)

| Category | Blocks |
|----------|--------|
| **Digital** | pinMode, digitalWrite, digitalRead |
| **Analog** | analogRead, analogWrite (PWM) |
| **Timing** | delay, millis, micros |
| **Serial** | Serial.begin, print, println, read |
| **Servo** | attach, write, read |
| **Motor** | DC motor control, stepper |
| **Display** | LCD, LED matrix, 7-segment |
| **Sensors** | Ultrasonic, IR, Temperature, Light |

#### 3.3 Stage Mode Protocol
- [ ] Real-time command protocol (already started)
- [ ] Sensor value streaming
- [ ] Motor/servo control
- [ ] LED/display control

---

### Phase 4: Machine Learning Environment

This is a major feature requiring a dedicated studio.

#### 4.1 ML Model Types

| Model Type | Description | Complexity |
|------------|-------------|------------|
| **Image Classifier** | Categorize images | Medium |
| **Object Detection** | Detect objects in image | High |
| **Pose Classifier** | Classify body poses (17 points) | High |
| **Hand Pose Classifier** | Hand gestures (21 points) | High |
| **Audio Classifier** | Classify sounds | Medium |
| **Text Classifier** | Sentiment/topic analysis | Medium |
| **Number Classifier** | Numeric data classification | Low |

#### 4.2 ML Workflow
```
┌─────────────┐    ┌─────────────┐    ┌─────────────┐    ┌─────────────┐
│  Collect    │ -> │   Train     │ -> │   Test      │ -> │   Export    │
│   Data      │    │   Model     │    │   Model     │    │  & Use      │
└─────────────┘    └─────────────┘    └─────────────┘    └─────────────┘
```

#### 4.3 Implementation Approach
- Use TensorFlow.js for browser-based training
- Pre-trained models (MobileNet, PoseNet, MediaPipe)
- Transfer learning for custom classifiers
- Export models for use in block coding

---

### Phase 5: Python Editor

#### 5.1 Features
- [ ] Syntax highlighting
- [ ] Auto-complete
- [ ] Error highlighting
- [ ] Line numbers
- [ ] Code folding
- [ ] Multiple tabs
- [ ] Console output panel
- [ ] Run/Stop buttons

#### 5.2 Python Libraries Support
- `pictoBlox` - Hardware control
- `time`, `random`, `math`
- `numpy`, `pandas` (for ML)
- `cv2` (OpenCV for vision)

#### 5.3 Implementation
- Use Monaco Editor (VS Code's editor)
- Python execution via Pyodide (WASM) or backend server

